 "notes": "The north-east shore of Ko Bangu (Similan 9): a reef from about 8 m, coral heads and a boulder cluster in the shallows, then the sand slope with the big granite boulders at 22–25 m and a single boulder at 18 m, the sand going on past 30 m, on the OpenStreetMap coastline, so positions are approximate. The three trees that name the site stand on the island's edge above the reef; their exact place is not known, so they are not drawn. Boulder depth 22 m from first-hand observation; garden eels on the sand.",
